{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Nisabha","html":"<article id='thag2.38'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 2.38 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 2.38 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Dukanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Twos </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Catutthavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Four </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Nisabhattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Nisabha </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Pañca kāmaguṇe hitvā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>One who’s given up the five sensual stimuli, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Piyarūpe manorame; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>so pleasing and delightful, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Saddhāya gharā nikkhamma, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and who’s left the home life out of faith—</span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Dukkhassantakaro bhave. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>let them make an end to suffering! </span></span></p>\n<p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Nābhinandāmi maraṇaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I don’t long for death; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>nābhinandāmi jīvitaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I don’t long for life; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Kālañca paṭikaṅkhāmi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I await my time, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>sampajāno patissato”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>aware and mindful. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Nisabho thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
